   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve given by \\( xe^{y} + y = 2 \\), along which \\( y \\) is a differentiable function of \\( x \\) near the point \\( (2, 0) \\). Find the value of \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} \\) at the point \\( (2, 0) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         4,
         27
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( xe^{y} + y = 2 \\) implicitly with respect to \\( x \\): \\( e^{y} + \\left(x e^{y} + 1\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\), so \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - \\frac{e^{y}}{x e^{y} + 1} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Divide",
               [
                  "Exp",
                  "y"
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     "x",
                     [
                        "Exp",
                        "y"
                     ]
                  ],
                  1
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{- e^{y}}{x e^{y} + 1} \\) again with the quotient rule, treating \\( y \\) as a function of \\( x \\): \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{- \\frac{dy}{dx} \\left(x e^{y} + 1\\right) e^{y} + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx} x e^{y} + e^{y}\\right) e^{y}}{\\left(x e^{y} + 1\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (2, 0) \\), \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - \\frac{1}{3} \\). Substitute this value and the coordinates into the second derivative.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            4,
            27
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{4}{27} \\) at \\( (2, 0) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            4,
            27
         ]
      }
